# Facebook Page credentials — shared by both the Phase 1 archiver (backfill.py)
# and the Phase 2 scheduler (scheduler.py). This project has its own Meta App
# and Page; never reuse another project's token or Page ID here.
#
# The token must be a Page Access Token (not a User token — a User token
# produces confusing (#200)/(#100) errors from scheduler.py that look like
# generic auth failures but actually mean the wrong token type was used).
# Scopes needed: pages_read_engagement + pages_show_list (Phase 1 archiving)
# and pages_manage_posts (Phase 2 scheduling).
FB_PAGE_ID=
FB_PAGE_TOKEN=

# Only needed for get_long_lived_token.py (occasional manual token refresh),
# never read by backfill.py or scheduler.py at runtime. Both are on the Meta
# App Dashboard's Settings > Basic page. FB_APP_SECRET is a real secret —
# never paste it in chat; add it here directly.
FB_APP_ID=
FB_APP_SECRET=

# Anthropic API — used by scheduler.py to draft post captions from structured
# source facts, when a queue item doesn't already carry a "message" (e.g. a
# repost of an archived post always has one, so this is only a fallback).
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Time of day (and timezone) selector.py schedules planned posts for.
# SCHEDULE_TIMEZONE=UTC
# SCHEDULE_HOUR=12

# Email summary — after `scheduler.py schedule` runs, notify.py emails
# MY_EMAIL_ADDRESS a list of the posts newly scheduled in that run, each with
# a best-effort preview link. Sent via smtplib (stdlib, no new dependency)
# through your own mail provider's SMTP — e.g. for Gmail, SMTP_HOST is
# smtp.gmail.com, SMTP_PORT is 587, and SMTP_PASSWORD must be a 16-character
# App Password (https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords), not your regular
# account password. If any of these are unset, the email is skipped (with a
# printed warning) rather than failing the schedule run.
MY_EMAIL_ADDRESS=
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_FROM=   # defaults to SMTP_USERNAME if unset

# Paid promotion / boosting (Marketing API) is a separate, manual-only
# concern per CLAUDE.md — it is never wired into scheduler.py's automated
# pipeline. If you add boosting later, give it its own ads-scoped token
# (ads_management/ads_read/business_management) here rather than reusing
# FB_PAGE_TOKEN above.
# FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=
# FB_ADS_TOKEN=
